[Desktop Entry]
# Spotify: its web player (open.spotify.com) in a window of its own — Brave's app window: no
# tabs, no address bar, tiled like every other window, through ~/.local/bin/brave-origin as
# all of Brave is. Free or Premium, signed in once (Brave keeps the login). It plays through
# Brave, so the bar's now-playing and its meter show it (Brave's media session over MPRIS,
# cava on the output) and the media keys work it. Spotify's player needs Widevine, which
# theme.sh switches on in Brave once (brave://settings → Widevine turns it off again).
# Its icon: Brave's own (theme.sh reads it from Brave's entry) — no Spotify icon is installed.
Type=Application
Name=Spotify
GenericName=Music Player
Comment=Spotify's web player, in a window of its own
Icon=@BRAVE_ICON@
Exec=@HOME@/.local/bin/brave-origin --app=https://open.spotify.com
Terminal=false
Categories=Audio;AudioVideo;Player;
Keywords=spotify;music;songs;podcasts;
